Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

For the time being we will be shipping mixed shipments of 2" 3G and 2" Upda=
ted Fittings.

When an order comes in for a 2" 3G fitting that we are out of we will be su=
bstituting a 2" Updated fitting.  Customer Service will alert the Regional =
Sales Manager (RSM) or Manufacturer's Representative (MR) that this is bein=
g done.

The RSM and the MR are responsible for alerting the customer and assuring t=
hat the end user is acquainted with the change and that the installation in=
struction is different.  The installation instructions for the 2" Updated f=
itting and the 2" 3G fitting are attached.  Further explanation may be foun=
d in the email below.  The RSM or MR should forward the installation instru=
ctions attached to the customer and the end user and provide whatever verba=
l support or site visit support is needed and practical.

Philmac has chosen to implement this design update to counter sensitivity t=
o proper installation rather than depend on the installation marks on the p=
revious product.  This is only for the 2" size.

For Acme Tees or Repair Couplings care must be exercised to assure that the=
 pipe is guided past the back of the second grip ring when loading the fitt=
ing on to the pipe prior to pulling the fitting back over the joint.  This =
would be done with the installer's free hand.  If pipe out of roundness mak=
es the joint "sticky" one can disassemble the joint end kits off the body l=
oading them and the body separately onto the pipe where they are reassemble=
d once the body is properly positioned.  The joint end kits are held as a u=
nit without loose pieces.

Call me if you have questions.

John



