Cc: Ed Eichmann; Stephen Tunstead (Stephen.Tunstead@philmac.com.au); 'Micha=
el Gathright'; John Inman; Kevin Evans; Steve Thompson
Subject: Info Blurt 37: Installation instructions for updated Philmac 2" IP=
S-OD Compression Fittings

All,

Attached is installation instruction for the 2" IPS-OD fitting that will be=
 replacing the 2" 3G fittings.  Smaller sizes will not be changed.

Installation is very similar except it is required that the nut be unscrewe=
d so that 3 threads are showing before pipe insertion.  If this is not done=
 the seal assembly will be compressed inboard and interfere with the pipe i=
nsertion.  The pipe encountering the seal could be felt as having stopped o=
ut when it has not.  Subsequent tightening will not actuate the seal proper=
ly resulting in a leak.

The nut will be tightened to the "vicinity" of the flange stop on the body.=
  There will be no installation marks on the fittings such as we have been =
applying to the 3G product it replaces.

Please inform your customers.  As this style fitting is supplied to your cu=
stomers our Customer Service will be alerting you.  For a time there will b=
e mixed shipments of old and new fittings.  Old fittings must be installed =
according to the second attachment.

John

